=/            V P O R T   W I R E   P R O T O C O L         \=
==============================================================

                       Version 0 (draft)


--[ 1. OVERVIEW ]----------------------------------------------

A client talks to vportd over a Unix domain socket
(SOCK_STREAM). Messages flow as a continuous byte stream; each
message is one frame made of an 8 byte header followed by a
payload whose size is fixed by the opcode.

All integers are little-endian. There is no padding.


--[ 2. HEADER ]------------------------------------------------

   0               2               4                       8
   +---------------+---------------+-----------------------+
   |    opcode     |     flags     |      payload_len      |
   |      u16      |      u16      |          u32          |
   +---------------+---------------+-----------------------+

  opcode       identifies the message, see section 4.
  flags        reserved, must be 0.
  payload_len  size of the payload in bytes. It must match the
               size defined for the opcode and must never
               exceed 1 MiB (1048576).


--[ 3. SESSION ]-----------------------------------------------

  1. The client connects to the socket.
  2. The client sends Hello with the version it speaks.
  3. The server answers Hello with the version it accepts.
  4. The client may then create portals and draw.

  Any message sent before Hello is a protocol violation. A
  second Hello is a protocol violation. A version mismatch
  closes the connection.

  The server reads the credentials of the peer (pid, uid, gid)
  from the kernel when the connection is accepted. These are
  never taken from the protocol.


--[ 4. MESSAGES ]----------------------------------------------

  Opcode  Name             Direction          Payload size
  ------  -----------      ---------------    ------------
  0x0001  Hello            both                4
  0x0010  InitPortal       client -> server   12
  0x0011  ClosePortal      client -> server    4
  0x0020  DrawRect         client -> server   16
  0x0040  Commit           client -> server    4
  0x0050  GrabKeyboard     client -> server    4
  0x0051  ReleaseKeyboard  client -> server    4
  0x8001  KeyEvent         server -> client   10
  0x8002  PointerButton    server -> client   10
  0x8003  FocusChanged     server -> client    5
  0x8004  GrabStatus       server -> client    5


  Hello (0x0001)

      +---------------+---------------+
      |    version    | capabilities  |
      |      u16      |      u16      |
      +---------------+---------------+

      version       protocol version, currently 1.
      capabilities  reserved, must be 0.


  InitPortal (0x0010)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |       x       |       y       |
      |      i16      |      i16      |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |       w       |       h       |
      |      u16      |      u16      |
      +---------------+---------------+

      Creates a portal owned by the calling client. The id is
      chosen by the client and must be unused.


  ClosePortal (0x0011)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +-------------------------------+

      Destroys a portal and everything drawn in it.


  DrawRect (0x0020)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |       x       |       y       |
      |      i16      |      i16      |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |       w       |       h       |
      |      u16      |      u16      |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |             rgba              |
      |              u32              |
      +-------------------------------+

      Queues a filled rectangle, relative to the portal.
      Colour is 0xRRGGBBAA. Nothing is shown until Commit.


  Commit (0x0040)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +-------------------------------+

      Atomically replaces the visible frame of the portal with
      all commands queued since the previous Commit.

  GrabKeyboard (0x0050) and ReleaseKeyboard (0x0051)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +-------------------------------+


  KeyEvent (0x8001)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |   scancode    |   modifiers   |
      |      u16      |      u16      |
      +-------+-------+---------------+
      |pressed| repeat|
      |  u8   |  u8   |
      +-------+-------+

      scancode is a USB HID usage id (usage page 0x07), so it
      does not depend on the keyboard layout. Modifier bits:
      0x0001 shift, 0x0002 ctrl, 0x0004 alt.


  PointerButton (0x8002)

      +-------------------------------+
      |           portal_id           |
      |              u32              |
      +---------------+---------------+
      |       x       |       y       |
      |      i16      |      i16      |
      +-------+-------+
      |button |pressed|
      |  u8   |  u8   |
      +-------+-------+

      x and y are relative to the portal. Buttons: 1 left,
      2 middle, 3 right, 4 and 5 extra.


  FocusChanged (0x8003)

      +-------------------------------+-------+
      |           portal_id           |focused|
      |              u32              |  u8   |
      +-------------------------------+-------+


  GrabStatus (0x8004)

      +-------------------------------+-------+
      |           portal_id           | status|
      |              u32              |  u8   |
      +-------------------------------+-------+

      status: 0 denied, 1 granted, 2 released.

  Stacking order: portals are drawn in the order their clients
  connected and, inside one client, by ascending portal_id.
  Rectangles are clipped to the bounds of their portal and to
  the screen.


--[ 5. INPUT, FOCUS AND KEYBOARD GRAB ]-----------------------

  Focus. At most one portal has keyboard focus. A new portal
  takes focus unless a keyboard grab is held. A pointer button
  press inside a portal gives it focus, unless a grab is held.
  When the focused portal goes away, the topmost remaining
  portal takes focus. The old and the new owner are told with
  FocusChanged.

  Pointer events. PointerButton goes to the topmost portal
  under the pointer. A keyboard grab does not affect it.

  Keyboard grab. A client asks for exclusive keyboard input
  with GrabKeyboard and the server answers with GrabStatus.
  The rules are strict:

    - The uid of the peer, read from the kernel with
      SO_PEERCRED, must be in the grab policy. By default the
      policy is uid 0 and the uid vportd runs as. The
      environment variable VPORT_GRAB_UIDS (comma separated
      uids) replaces that list.
    - Only one grab exists at a time. A second request is
      denied; a grab is never taken away from its holder.

  While a grab is held, all keyboard events go to the portal
  of the holder, which also gets focus. The grab ends with
  ReleaseKeyboard, when the portal is closed, or when the
  client disconnects.

  A client that sends a server-only message (opcode 0x8000 or
  higher) is disconnected.


--[ 6. LIMITS ]------------------------------------------------

  Maximum payload size                  1 MiB
  Maximum clients                          64
  Maximum portals per client                8
  Maximum uncommitted rectangles per portal 4096


--[ 7. ERRORS ]------------------------------------------------

  The server does not send error messages. A client that
  breaks the protocol is disconnected, and the reason is
  written to the server log. Causes include:

      - unknown opcode
      - payload size different from the one the opcode needs
      - payload larger than the maximum
      - message before Hello, or Hello twice
      - unsupported protocol version
      - unknown portal id, or portal id already in use
      - any limit in section 5 exceeded


--[ 8. PLANNED ]-----------------------------------------------

  ShowText, StreamBuffer and server to client Event messages
  (input, focus, portal closed) are not part of version 0.


